//? Title: DDPM: Explicit Noising, Noise Prediction and Ancestral Sampling
//? Subtitle: Native tensor components with editable training and sampling loops
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
This report preserves the original ddpm experiment and moves reusable tensor operations into datamunge. Parameter stores, objectives, minibatch loops, optimizer writes and sampling trajectories are visible in the complete program.
)
\toc

> Method, preserved protocol and observed limitations

[Ho, Jain and Abbeel, Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models (2020)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.11239) gives the denoising formulation. This compact experiment predicts noise with a 72-to 32-to 32-to 64 SiLU MLP:5504 values in six leaves. It uses 32 cosine levels, continuous half-pixel-resized8x8 MNIST and fixed-final three-epoch Adam training:1000 fitting,200 validation and 200 test images,96 optimizer writes. No threshold is applied.

The caller constructs x_t=sqrt(alpha_bar_t)*x_0+sqrt(1-alpha_bar_t)*epsilon and minimizes mean squared noise error. Sampling predicts epsilon, infers and clips x_0 to[-1,1], then applies the fixed-variance posterior with explicit innovations. At level0 posterior variance is zero. The program checks this exactly, along with checkpoint restore, repeatability, time conditioning and frozen inference.

Test epsilon MSE is 0.838227928, above the fitting-only Gaussian pixel-prior baseline0.233514349 and below the zero predictor1.014657692. The baseline shortfall is retained; this short experiment does not demonstrate competitive image generation. Test clipped-clean MSE is 0.640106230. The terminal conditional-prior KL diagnostic is not a trained likelihood.

> Follow the state through one model operation

The method diagram separates the explicitly supplied state and conditioning from the predictor and the single transition. The caller owns repeated transitions and training.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ddpm_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
